review_text:
The most common question I've been asked since Black Summer came out is "Is it as good as The Walking Dead?". Whilst I don't think that's a fair comparison because of the sheer budget difference, I do think it's an easy question to answer; no. It's not. But it's decent at what it does.The premise is simple; a virus is spreading (airborn) and turning people into ravenous creatures which are almost identical to the zombies seen in Dawn Of The Dead(2004). The story itself is about people trying to get from A to B (it's really that simple). A man trying to find his sister and children, a mother searching for her daughter etc. Whilst the little stories it tells are okay, I found myself been taken out of the experience since the movie has short segments per episode but I can overlook this.
Whilst I do think Black Summer is worth a watch, I don't think it's even close to other series we've already got. The problem is that it does nothing new, doesn't explore anything new or tell a new kind of story. It's generic but having said that, it's generic done well which is why I think it's worth a watch.TLDR;
Nothing new, ground-breaking or overly memorable but something decent to watch for fans of 28 Days/Weeks Later, The Walking Dead, Dawn Of The Dead etc.
